repaired.reasoning:
Reproduced in a private copy: each of the six single mutations left pressable_test.dart and widgets_test.dart green (`_ring = _showsFocus` removed from didUpdateWidget, same line removed from initState, `&& !event.synthesized` dropped, `event is KeyDownEvent` dropped, `_listeners.contains(listener)` removed, `|| !mounted` removed from the hover callback).

Five of the six are now killed by new tests; I added tests only and did not edit any existing test body (the suggested two expects are covered by the first new test instead):
- 'a focused control that is given another focus node loses its ring with the node' (ring reset on swap);
- 'a control that is given a node that has the focus shows it as the last input says' (the same line in the other direction and after a mouse press; kills `_ring = false` and `_ring = _node.hasPrimaryFocus` too);
- 'a control built on a node that has the focus shows it from its first frame, as the last input says' (initState line, keyboard and mouse);
- 'a key that repeats or is let go is not pressed again' (Shift held during a click, repeat event, then release);
- 'a key event that only mends the record of the keyboard is not a key press' (synthesized KeyDown/KeyUp fed to HardwareKeyboard);
- 'a hovered control that is disabled and scrolled away in the same frame is left alone' (hover `!mounted`: without the guard the detector's post-frame report calls setState on a disposed State). The guard is reachable only when a control is updated and unmounted in one frame; LayoutBuilder cannot do that in this SDK (it has its own BuildScope), a lazy list that garbage-collects the item during layout can, hence the `_lazyList` helper.

Not pinned, on purpose: `_listeners.contains(listener)` in `_KkFocusVisibility._notify` (and the list copy next to it). It cannot be reached through the public API: the only listeners are `_syncRing`, which only calls setState, so nothing can add or remove a listener during the walk. I kept it as the framework's own idiom (FocusManager._notifyHighlightModeListeners has the same two lines) and said so in a comment; deleting both would be behaviour-neutral today.

Key repeats were undecided by the tests; I pinned the existing behaviour (a repeat is not a press) because a held modifier repeats on Windows and counting repeats would bring the ring back right after a Shift+click.

Source change in this snapshot is comments only: three comments saying what the hover guard, the key conditions and the listener walk are for.
